                <pb facs="0525" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg453"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6369/268.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Merry.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-11-12"><hi rendition="#italic">November 12,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Knox informs Mr. Merry that the department hopes that Costa Rica will
                    continue to take every means at her disposal to compel the faithful observance
                    of the treaties of Washington.</p>
            </div>
